1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,800
How advanced could a civilisation become?

2
00:00:04,060 --> 00:00:09,070
In 1964, the Soviet astronomer Nikolai
Kardashev suggested a simple measure:

3
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:11,330
how much energy it can use.

4
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:15,060
Carl Sagan later made it a sliding scale.

5
00:00:15,305 --> 00:00:19,795
Each type uses about ten billion
times more power than the one before.

6
00:00:20,883 --> 00:00:25,413
A Type One civilisation uses power
on the scale of its whole planet.

7
00:00:25,683 --> 00:00:28,633
On Sagan's scale,
that's ten to the sixteen watts.

8
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:30,920
We're not there yet.

9
00:00:31,235 --> 00:00:35,245
In 2021, humanity used
about nineteen terawatts.

10
00:00:35,605 --> 00:00:38,575
That makes us roughly Type
zero point seven three.

11
00:00:39,883 --> 00:00:43,513
A Type Two civilisation
harnesses its entire star.

12
00:00:43,833 --> 00:00:48,243
One idea is a swarm of collectors
around it, known as a Dyson sphere.

13
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:52,220
A Type Three civilisation
commands a whole galaxy:

14
00:00:52,850 --> 00:00:54,500
the light of billions of stars.

15
00:00:55,683 --> 00:00:57,293
That's where Kardashev stopped.

16
00:00:57,613 --> 00:01:00,963
Everything above Type Three is
speculation by later thinkers,

17
00:01:01,413 --> 00:01:02,423
and they don't agree.

18
00:01:03,483 --> 00:01:05,733
Type Four would reach beyond its galaxy.

19
00:01:06,283 --> 00:01:11,253
Physicist Michio Kaku imagined it
drawing energy from between the galaxies.

20
00:01:11,728 --> 00:01:14,138
Popular versions say the whole universe.

21
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:18,733
Type Five, in popular versions,
spans many universes:

22
00:01:19,303 --> 00:01:20,153
a multiverse.

23
00:01:20,573 --> 00:01:25,323
Futurist Zoltán Galántai's scale
calls this stage technically immortal.

24
00:01:26,417 --> 00:01:30,307
Types Six and Seven come mostly
from internet videos and fiction.

25
00:01:30,647 --> 00:01:32,497
Six masters space and time.

26
00:01:32,777 --> 00:01:35,787
Seven is god-like,
able to create universes.

27
00:01:36,317 --> 00:01:38,687
No scientific paper defines them.

28
00:01:39,617 --> 00:01:43,147
So on the real scale,
we're still climbing towards Type One.

29
00:01:43,397 --> 00:01:46,447
Everything beyond that
is imagination, for now.

